#uuid "b8c7b5c0-57d6-5e10-9424-b187294f0724" :question/math-academy-id "q-326250" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}-2,\\,y=\\frac{t-1}{t+1},\\,0\\le t\\le 5.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-\\frac{3}{2}$ | $2$ | $\\frac{23}{2}$ | $30$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $0$ | {{field-2}} | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(5),$ we substitute $t=5$ into $x=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(5)=\\frac{1}{2}(5)^{3}-2=\\frac{125}{2}-\\frac{4}{2}=\\frac{121}{2}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $y=\\frac{t-1}{t+1}.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(2)=\\frac{2-1}{2+1}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(5),$ we substitute $t=5$ into $y=\\frac{t-1}{t+1}.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(0)=\\frac{5-1}{5+1}=\\frac{4}{6}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-\\frac{3}{2}$ | $2$ | $\\frac{23}{2}$ | $30$ | $\\frac{121}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302273 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dea4c418-a2a3-5eb1-914f-abfb1e44f530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301065}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301065} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f6a1cf6-f1e9-5324-a0cd-8de8748825b8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ca4294-13f5-564a-9c61-bfe51e2f5894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300288}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300288} :answer-field/id #uuid "af402e53-ece3-5170-871d-14635b65690e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301800} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dbec592-362f-5cb8-838b-38b868c54f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300263}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300263} :answer-field/id #uuid "d785ba22-7770-5336-8681-5b6890e427ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301920}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9505d474-040a-5e78-97f1-c782cc218ed5" :question/math-academy-id "q-326251" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{\\,t+4\\,},\\,y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t,\\,-3\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-1}} | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{5}$ | $\\sqrt{6}$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{33}{2}$ | $8$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(-3),$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $x=\\sqrt{\\,t+4\\,}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(-3)=\\sqrt{-3+4}=\\sqrt{1}=1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(-1),$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(-1)=\\frac{3}{2}(-1)^{2}-(-1)=\\frac{3}{2}+1=\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{2}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(2)=\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{2}-(2)=6-2=4.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{5}$ | $\\sqrt{6}$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{33}{2}$ | $8$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $4$ |"}]}
